**1. Overview & Architecture Goals**

\[PLATFORM NAME\] is a multi-tenant SaaS platform. Every company that
subscribes is a tenant --- an isolated, independent business environment
sharing the same underlying infrastructure. This document defines how
that isolation is achieved, how the system scales, how security is
enforced, and how the cross-tenant collaboration feature bridges two
separate tenants on shared projects.

**1.1 Core Architecture Goals**

-   Complete data isolation --- no tenant can ever access another
    tenant\'s data

-   Horizontal scalability --- the platform can grow from 10 tenants to
    10,000 without architectural rework

-   Single codebase --- all tenants run on the same application; no
    per-tenant deployments

-   Configurable per tenant --- branding, workflows, custom fields,
    integrations differ per tenant without code changes

-   Secure by design --- tenant isolation enforced at the database
    layer, not just the application layer

-   Cross-tenant collaboration --- a governed, permission-controlled
    data bridge for GC-to-Sub project connections

-   Performance isolation --- one high-traffic tenant cannot degrade the
    experience for others

**1.2 Tenancy Model Selection**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Model**        **Description**       **Selected?**   **Reason**
  ---------------- --------------------- --------------- -----------------------
  Separate         Each tenant gets      No              Operationally expensive
  database per     their own database                    --- backup, migration,
  tenant           instance                              and schema updates
                                                         multiply with tenant
                                                         count.

  Separate schema  Same DB server, each  No              Better but still
  per tenant       tenant gets their own                 creates migration
                   schema                                complexity and limits
                                                         cross-tenant query
                                                         capability.

  Shared schema    All tenants in the    YES             Industry standard for
  with tenant_id   same tables, every                    SaaS at this scale.
                   row tagged with                       Simple migrations,
                   tenant_id                             efficient
                                                         infrastructure,
                                                         enforced at DB layer
                                                         via RLS.
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Selected Model: Shared schema with tenant_id isolation. Every table
  includes a tenant_id column. Row-level security (RLS) policies enforce
  that queries can only return rows where tenant_id matches the
  authenticated session\'s tenant. This is enforced at the database layer
  --- even a bug in application code cannot return another tenant\'s
  data.**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

