**4.2 API Gateway Responsibilities**

-   TLS termination --- all traffic decrypted at the gateway

-   JWT token validation --- every request must carry a valid, unexpired
    JWT

-   Tenant extraction --- tenant_id extracted from JWT and injected into
    request context

-   Rate limiting --- per-tenant rate limits enforced (1,000 req/min
    Professional, 5,000 Enterprise)

-   Request routing --- routes to appropriate backend service

-   DDoS protection and IP allowlisting for Super Admin endpoints

**4.3 Authentication & Session Management**

**JWT Token Structure**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| {                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| \"sub\": \"user_uuid\", // User ID                                    |
|                                                                       |
| \"tenant_id\": \"t_001\", // Tenant ID --- CRITICAL claim             |
|                                                                       |
| \"role\": \"project_manager\", // User role within tenant             |
|                                                                       |
| \"email\": \"pm@abcgc.com\",                                          |
|                                                                       |
| \"iat\": 1711900000, // Issued at                                     |
|                                                                       |
| \"exp\": 1711986400, // Expires (24hr web, 30d mobile)                |
|                                                                       |
| \"jti\": \"unique_token_id\" // JWT ID for revocation                 |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**Token Lifecycle**

-   Access token: 24-hour expiry for web, 30-day expiry for mobile

-   Refresh token: 90-day expiry, stored httpOnly cookie (web) or secure
    storage (mobile)

-   Token revocation: jti stored in Redis cache --- checked on every
    request

-   MFA: enforced before token issuance when tenant admin has enabled it

**4.4 File & Document Storage**

All tenant files stored in object storage with per-tenant path
isolation. Files exist in one of two prefixes --- quarantine (during
scanning) or live (accessible). No file is accessible until it has been
scanned.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| /{tenant_id}/quarantine/{upload_id}/{filename} ← Held during scanning |
|                                                                       |
| /{tenant_id}/live/projects/{project_id}/plans/{filename}              |
|                                                                       |
| /{tenant_id}/live/projects/{project_id}/photos/{filename}             |
|                                                                       |
| /{tenant_id}/live/projects/{project_id}/documents/{filename}          |
|                                                                       |
| /{tenant_id}/live/company/templates/{filename}                        |
|                                                                       |
| /{tenant_id}/live/company/logos/{filename}                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

File access is never exposed directly by path. All file URLs are
pre-signed URLs generated by the API with a 15-minute expiry.

