**4.6 Background Job Architecture & Tenant Context**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Every background job must carry tenant_id in the SQS message envelope
  and apply withTenantContext() before any DB query. Superadmin bypass in
  job workers is prohibited. --- T-10**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.6.1 Overview**

Background jobs (QuickBooks sync, email delivery, report generation,
notification dispatch, data export) are processed asynchronously via SQS
queues and Lambda/ECS workers. Because these jobs have no JWT token,
tenant context must be carried in the job message envelope itself.

**4.6.2 Job Message Envelope (Standard)**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| {                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| \"job_id\": \"uuid-v4\",                                              |
|                                                                       |
| \"job_type\": \"quickbooks_sync \| email_delivery \| report_generate  |
| \| notification_dispatch \| data_export\",                            |
|                                                                       |
| \"tenant_id\": \"t_001\",                                             |
|                                                                       |
| \"initiated_by\": \"user_uuid \| system\",                            |
|                                                                       |
| \"enqueued_at\": \"2026-03-13T10:00:00Z\",                            |
|                                                                       |
| \"payload\": { /\* job-specific data \*/ }                            |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

tenant_id is set by the API layer at the time the job is enqueued. It is
never set by the job worker itself. The worker treats it as
authoritative.

**4.6.3 Worker Tenant Context Pattern**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| async function processJob(message) {                                  |
|                                                                       |
| const { job_id, job_type, tenant_id, payload } = message;             |
|                                                                       |
| if (!tenant_id) {                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| logger.error({ job_id, job_type }, \'Job message missing tenant_id    |
| --- dead-lettering\');                                                |
|                                                                       |
| throw new Error(\'MISSING_TENANT_ID\');                               |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| await withTenantContext(tenant_id, async () =\> {                     |
|                                                                       |
| await executeJob(job_type, payload);                                  |
|                                                                       |
| });                                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

Jobs that arrive without a tenant_id are rejected to the dead-letter
queue immediately --- never processed with a superadmin bypass.

**4.6.4 Queue Structure**

  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Queue**                **Purpose**                        **DLQ
                                                              Retention**
  ------------------------ ---------------------------------- --------------
  platform-jobs-standard   General async jobs ---             14 days
                           notifications, emails, reports     

  platform-jobs-sync       Integration sync jobs ---          14 days
                           QuickBooks, DocuSign               

  platform-jobs-export     Data export and large report       14 days
                           generation                         

  platform-jobs-dlq        Dead-letter queue --- all failed   30 days
                           jobs land here                     
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.6.5 Failure & Retry Behavior**

-   Standard retry: 3 attempts with exponential backoff (30s, 2min,
    10min)

-   After 3 failures: message moves to dead-letter queue (DLQ)

-   DLQ alerts: CloudWatch alarm fires when DLQ depth \> 0 --- on-call
    engineer notified

-   DLQ messages are inspectable and replayable by super admin --- never
    auto-discarded

-   Failed integration jobs trigger in-app notification to tenant admin

**4.7 API Versioning Strategy**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **All API endpoints launch under /v1/. Breaking changes introduce a new
  version prefix. Deprecated versions supported for minimum 6 months. All
  clients must send User-Agent with app version. --- T-11**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.7.1 Versioning Mechanism**

All API endpoints are versioned by URL path prefix. The full v1.0 API
launches under /v1/:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| https://api.platformname.com/v1/projects                              |
|                                                                       |
| https://api.platformname.com/v1/tenants/{tenant_id}/users             |
|                                                                       |
| https://api.platformname.com/v1/financials/invoices                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.7.2 What Constitutes a Breaking Change**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Change Type**            **Example**              **Breaking?**
  -------------------------- ------------------------ ---------------------
  Removing a field from a    Removing                 YES
  response                   project.job_number       

  Renaming a field           status → project_status  YES

  Changing a field\'s data   contract_value string →  YES
  type                       integer                  

  Removing an endpoint       DELETE /v1/invoices/{id} YES
                             removed                  

  Adding a new optional      Adding                   NO
  field                      project.weather_zone     

  Adding a new optional      Adding                   NO
  request parameter          ?include_archived=true   

  Adding a new endpoint      New /v1/lien-waivers     NO

  Expanding an enum with new Adding status: on_hold   NO
  values                                              
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.7.3 Deprecation Policy**

-   /v1/ supported for minimum 6 months after /v2/ launches

-   Deprecated endpoints return Deprecation, Sunset, and Link response
    headers from day of new version launch

-   Tenant admins receive in-app banner when their app version is
    calling a deprecated endpoint

-   At sunset date: deprecated endpoints return 410 Gone with migration
    guide URL --- never silently removed

**4.7.4 Client Version Tracking**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| \# Web app                                                            |
|                                                                       |
| User-Agent: PlatformWeb/1.0.0                                         |
|                                                                       |
| \# Mobile app                                                         |
|                                                                       |
| User-Agent: PlatformMobile/2.3.1 (iOS 17.4)                           |
|                                                                       |
| User-Agent: PlatformMobile/2.3.1 (Android 14)                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

The API Gateway logs the User-Agent on every request. This feeds a Super
Admin console dashboard showing active client version distribution.
Requests missing a User-Agent header are accepted but flagged in logs
--- field workers on old app versions must not be locked out.

**4.8 Offline Conflict Resolution**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Optimistic locking via version integer trigger. Tiered field policy.
  Side-by-side resolution UI. --- T-12, T-13, T-14**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.8.1 The Conflict Scenario**

The mobile app is offline-first. Field workers write to local SQLite
(WatermelonDB) without connectivity. When connectivity is restored, the
sync queue processes local writes against the server. A conflict occurs
when the server record has been modified by another user while the field
worker was offline.

**4.8.2 Optimistic Locking --- Data Model**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| \-- Every mobile-writable table carries a version integer             |
|                                                                       |
| ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1;      |
|                                                                       |
| ALTER TABLE daily_reports ADD COLUMN version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT |
| 1;                                                                    |
|                                                                       |
| ALTER TABLE inspections ADD COLUMN version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT   |
| 1;                                                                    |
|                                                                       |
| ALTER TABLE invoices ADD COLUMN version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1;   |
|                                                                       |
| ALTER TABLE punch_list_items ADD COLUMN version INTEGER NOT NULL      |
| DEFAULT 1;                                                            |
|                                                                       |
| ALTER TABLE change_orders ADD COLUMN version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT |
| 1;                                                                    |
|                                                                       |
| \-- Version incremented by DB trigger --- never trusted from client   |
| payload                                                               |
|                                                                       |
| CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION increment_version()                        |
|                                                                       |
| RETURNS TRIGGER AS \$\$                                               |
|                                                                       |
| BEGIN                                                                 |
|                                                                       |
| NEW.version = OLD.version + 1;                                        |
|                                                                       |
| NEW.updated_at = NOW();                                               |
|                                                                       |
| RETURN NEW;                                                           |
|                                                                       |
| END;                                                                  |
|                                                                       |
| \$\$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.8.3 Sync Write Protocol**

When the mobile app syncs an offline write, it includes the version it
held when the record was last fetched. The server checks: if versions
match, write succeeds. If server version is higher, 409 Conflict is
returned with the current server state.

**4.8.4 Tiered Field Sensitivity Policy**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Tier**      **Field Types**  **Examples**               **Conflict Behavior**
  ------------- ---------------- -------------------------- ---------------------
  Financial     Monetary values, invoice_amount,            Strict --- conflict
                contract amounts contract_value,            always surfaced to
                                 budget_allocated           user. Write blocked
                                                            until resolved.

  Operational   Status fields,   task_status,               Conflict surfaced to
                scheduled dates, scheduled_date,            user. Write blocked
                assignments      assigned_to                until resolved.

  Append-only   Photos, notes,   photos\[\], field_notes,   Last write wins ---
                daily report     daily_report_entries\[\]   additive by nature.
                entries                                     No conflict possible.

  System        Ownership and    tenant_id, created_at,     Server always wins
                integrity fields version, created_by        --- client values
                                                            ignored on sync.
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.8.5 Conflict Resolution UI --- Side-by-Side**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐                   |
|                                                                       |
| │ ⚠️ Sync Conflict --- Task: Rough Electrical │                       |
|                                                                       |
| │ Someone updated this while you were offline │                       |
|                                                                       |
| ├────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┤                   |
|                                                                       |
| │ YOUR VERSION │ CURRENT VERSION │                                    |
|                                                                       |
| │ (offline) │ (server) │                                              |
|                                                                       |
| ├────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤                   |
|                                                                       |
| │ Status │ Status │                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| │ ● Complete \[✓\] │ ○ Blocked │                                      |
|                                                                       |
| ├────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤                   |
|                                                                       |
| │ Notes │ Notes │                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| │ ● \"Wiring done\" │ ○ \"Waiting on inspect\" \[✓\] │                |
|                                                                       |
| ├────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┤                   |
|                                                                       |
| │ \[Cancel\] \[Apply My Selections\] │                                |
|                                                                       |
| └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

-   Only fields that differ between client and server are shown ---
    identical fields merged silently

-   Financial tier fields show a warning label: \'This affects billing
    --- choose carefully\'

-   Field worker must select a value for each conflicting field before
    submission

-   \'Cancel\' leaves the record in the sync queue --- other records
    continue syncing normally

-   Unresolved conflicts surfaced in a \'Sync Issues\' badge on the
    mobile app home screen

**4.8.6 Conflict Logging**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| CREATE TABLE offline_conflicts (                                      |
|                                                                       |
| id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),                        |
|                                                                       |
| tenant_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES tenants(id),                       |
|                                                                       |
| user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),                           |
|                                                                       |
| table_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,                                     |
|                                                                       |
| record_id UUID NOT NULL,                                              |
|                                                                       |
| client_version INTEGER NOT NULL,                                      |
|                                                                       |
| server_version INTEGER NOT NULL,                                      |
|                                                                       |
| conflicting_fields JSONB,                                             |
|                                                                       |
| resolution JSONB,                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| resolved_by VARCHAR(20), \-- \'user\' \| \'system\'                   |
|                                                                       |
| created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),                                 |
|                                                                       |
| resolved_at TIMESTAMPTZ                                               |
|                                                                       |
| );                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.9 Inbound Webhook Architecture**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **One endpoint per provider. Signature validation first --- before any
  DB write. Async processing. Event ID deduplication. --- T-18, T-19,
  T-20**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.9.1 Webhook Endpoints**

  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Provider**   **Endpoint**              **Registered Where**
  -------------- ------------------------- ---------------------------------
  Stripe         POST /v1/webhooks/stripe  Stripe Dashboard → Webhooks

  QuickBooks     POST                      QuickBooks Developer Portal
                 /v1/webhooks/quickbooks   

  DocuSign       POST                      DocuSign Connect configuration
                 /v1/webhooks/docusign     

  Twilio         POST /v1/webhooks/twilio  Twilio Console → Messaging
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.9.2 Receiver Handler Pattern**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| async function handleWebhook(provider, req, res) {                    |
|                                                                       |
| // Step 1 --- Validate signature (provider-specific) FIRST            |
|                                                                       |
| const isValid = validateSignature(provider, req);                     |
|                                                                       |
| if (!isValid) {                                                       |
|                                                                       |
| logger.warn({ provider, ip: req.ip }, \'Webhook signature validation  |
| failed\');                                                            |
|                                                                       |
| return res.status(403).end();                                         |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| const eventId = extractEventId(provider, req.body);                   |
|                                                                       |
| const eventType = extractEventType(provider, req.body);               |
|                                                                       |
| // Step 2 --- Persist raw event                                       |
|                                                                       |
| await db.query(\`                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| INSERT INTO inbound_webhooks (provider, event_id, event_type,         |
| raw_payload)                                                          |
|                                                                       |
| VALUES (\$1, \$2, \$3, \$4)                                           |
|                                                                       |
| ON CONFLICT (provider, event_id) DO NOTHING                           |
|                                                                       |
| \`, \[provider, eventId, eventType, req.body\]);                      |
|                                                                       |
| // Step 3 --- Enqueue background job                                  |
|                                                                       |
| await sqs.sendMessage({ QueueUrl: WEBHOOK_QUEUE_URL,                  |
|                                                                       |
| MessageBody: JSON.stringify({ provider, event_id: eventId }),         |
|                                                                       |
| MessageDeduplicationId: \`\${provider}-\${eventId}\`                  |
|                                                                       |
| });                                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| // Step 4 --- Acknowledge immediately (\<500ms)                       |
|                                                                       |
| return res.status(200).end();                                         |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.9.3 Inbound Webhooks Table**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| CREATE TABLE inbound_webhooks (                                       |
|                                                                       |
| id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),                        |
|                                                                       |
| provider VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,                                        |
|                                                                       |
| event_id VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,                                       |
|                                                                       |
| event_type VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,                                     |
|                                                                       |
| tenant_id UUID REFERENCES tenants(id),                                |
|                                                                       |
| raw_payload JSONB NOT NULL,                                           |
|                                                                       |
| status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT \'pending\',                      |
|                                                                       |
| attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,                                  |
|                                                                       |
| last_error TEXT,                                                      |
|                                                                       |
| received_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),                       |
|                                                                       |
| processed_at TIMESTAMPTZ,                                             |
|                                                                       |
| UNIQUE (provider, event_id)                                           |
|                                                                       |
| );                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.9.4 Key Events Per Provider**

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Provider**   **Event**                       **Platform Action**
  -------------- ------------------------------- -----------------------------------
  Stripe         invoice.payment_succeeded       Mark invoice paid, trigger
                                                 QuickBooks sync

  Stripe         customer.subscription.deleted   Move tenant to cancelled state

  QuickBooks     dataChangeEvent (Invoice)       Sync invoice status changes back to
                                                 platform

  DocuSign       envelope-completed              Mark contract signed, notify
                                                 project team

  DocuSign       envelope-declined               Alert contract owner, update
                                                 contract status

  Twilio         delivered                       Confirm SMS delivery, update
                                                 notification log

  Twilio         failed                          Log delivery failure, trigger
                                                 fallback notification
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.10 External Integration Resilience**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Exponential backoff with jitter. Per-integration circuit breaker.
  Integration failures are never silent. --- T-21, T-22, T-23**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.10.1 Core Principle**

The platform always works. Integration failures affect sync and delivery
--- never core data entry, project management, or financial record
keeping. A QuickBooks outage means sync is delayed, not that the
platform is down.

**4.10.2 Retry Strategy --- Exponential Backoff with Jitter**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| const RETRY_SCHEDULE = \[30, 120, 600, 3600, 21600\]; // seconds      |
|                                                                       |
| // ±20% random jitter applied to each interval to prevent retry       |
| storms                                                                |
|                                                                       |
| // Attempt 1 failure → retry in \~30s (24--36s)                       |
|                                                                       |
| // Attempt 2 failure → retry in \~2min (96--144s)                     |
|                                                                       |
| // Attempt 3 failure → retry in \~10min (8--12min)                    |
|                                                                       |
| // Attempt 4 failure → retry in \~1hr (48--72min)                     |
|                                                                       |
| // Attempt 5 failure → retry in \~6hr (4.8--7.2hr)                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.10.3 Failure Classification**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Failure Type**   **HTTP /        **Retry Behavior**
                     Error**         
  ------------------ --------------- ------------------------------------
  Transient / server 500, 502, 503,  Retry with backoff --- likely
  error              504             recovers

  Rate limited       429             Retry after Retry-After header
                                     interval

  Timeout            Network timeout Retry with backoff

  Authentication     401, 403        Do NOT retry --- alert tenant admin
  failure                            immediately

  Not found          404             Do NOT retry --- log and mark failed

  Bad request        400             Do NOT retry --- alert engineering
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.10.4 Circuit Breaker States**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| CLOSED (normal) ──── 5 consecutive failures ──→ OPEN (blocked)        |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| 5-min recovery timeout                                                |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| probe succeeds ←── HALF-OPEN ←──────┘                                 |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| CLOSED ←── (circuit closes, failures reset to 0)                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

Circuit breaker state stored in Redis --- shared across all worker
instances. Opens after 5 consecutive failures. Half-open probe allowed
after 5-minute recovery timeout. Authentication failures bypass circuit
breaker and go directly to tenant notification.

**4.10.5 User Communication Tiers**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Trigger**           **Communication**               **Audience**
  --------------------- ------------------------------- -----------------
  First retry cycle     In-app notification:            Tenant admin
  fails (attempt 2)     \'QuickBooks sync is            
                        experiencing issues ---         
                        retrying automatically.\'       

  Attempt 4 fails       In-app notification + email:    Tenant admin
  (\~1hr of retrying)   \'Sync has been failing for     
                        over an hour. Contact support   
                        if this persists.\'             

  Circuit breaker opens In-app banner showing last      All tenant users
                        successful sync time and        
                        current status                  

  Authentication        Immediate notification + email: Tenant admin
  failure               \'Connection lost --- please    
                        reconnect your account.\' with  
                        reconnect link                  

  Circuit closes / sync In-app notification: \'Sync has Tenant admin
  recovers              recovered. All pending changes  
                        have been synced.\'             
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.10.6 Graceful Degradation**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Integration**   **Degraded Behavior**
  ----------------- -------------------------------------------------------
  QuickBooks        Platform continues normally. Invoices and financial
                    records created and stored. Sync queue accumulates and
                    replays on recovery. Users see \'last synced\'
                    timestamp.

  DocuSign          Contracts managed locally. E-signature requests queued.
                    Manual signature workflow available as fallback.

  Stripe            Existing subscriptions unaffected. New subscription
                    changes queued. Tenant admin notified if billing action
                    is delayed.

  Twilio            SMS notifications fall back to email. Push
                    notifications (APNs/FCM) unaffected. Users notified SMS
                    is temporarily unavailable.
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.11 File Upload Security**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **All uploads quarantined before accessible. Triple validation.
  Per-type size limits. Per-tier storage quotas. --- T-27, T-28, T-29,
  T-30**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.11.1 Upload Pipeline**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Client → API Layer → Triple Validation → Write to /quarantine/ → Scan |
| → Move to /live/                                                      |
|                                                                       |
| Triple Validation (all three must pass):                              |
|                                                                       |
| 1\. Extension allowlist check                                         |
|                                                                       |
| 2\. Magic byte validation (actual file content matches extension)     |
|                                                                       |
| 3\. Content-Type header must match expected MIME types                |
|                                                                       |
| If any validation fails → 422 Unprocessable Entity (before storage    |
| write)                                                                |
|                                                                       |
| If scan passes → move to /live/ → generate pre-signed URL → notify    |
| via WebSocket                                                         |
|                                                                       |
| If scan fails → delete from quarantine → notify uploader → log        |
| security event                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.11.2 Permitted File Types**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Extension**   **Magic        **MIME Types**                       **Max
                  Bytes**                                             Size**
  --------------- -------------- ------------------------------------ -----------
  pdf             %PDF           application/pdf                      50MB

  jpg/jpeg        FF D8          image/jpeg                           25MB

  png             89 50          image/png                            25MB

  heic            varies         image/heic                           25MB

  dwg             AC10           image/vnd.dwg                        250MB

  docx            50 4B          application/vnd.openxmlformats\...   50MB

  mp4             varies         video/mp4                            500MB
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.11.3 Per-Tenant Storage Quotas**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Tier**        **Storage       **At 80%**           **At 100%**
                  Quota**                              
  --------------- --------------- -------------------- --------------------
  Starter         10GB            In-app warning to    Uploads blocked
                                  admin                

  Professional    50GB            In-app warning to    Uploads blocked
                                  admin                

  Business        250GB           In-app warning to    Uploads blocked
                                  admin                

  Enterprise      Unlimited       Alert at 500GB+      No hard cap
                                  (monitoring)         
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.11.4 Scanner Provider Interface**

The scanner is behind a provider-agnostic interface. SCANNER_PROVIDER
environment variable determines the active provider. No upload handler
code changes required when migrating from Cloudmersive to GuardDuty at
Stage 3.

-   Stage 1--2 (DigitalOcean): Cloudmersive Virus Scan API (\~\$0/mo
    free tier, \~\$50/mo paid)

-   Stage 3+ (AWS): GuardDuty Malware Protection for S3 (\~\$0.60/GB
    scanned)

**4.12 Audit Log Architecture**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Six-category comprehensive log. Append-only, hash-chained for tamper
  evidence. Tenant admin read-only access. 7-year retention. SOC 2
  evidence begins at v1.0 launch. --- T-31, T-32, T-33, T-34**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.12.1 Core Principles**

-   Entries are append-only --- never updated, never deleted

-   Every entry is hash-chained to the previous --- tampering is
    detectable

-   All entries stored in English regardless of user locale

-   Logging happens in the same transaction as the action --- no log
    entry means the action didn\'t happen

-   Two scopes: tenant-level (visible to tenant admins) and
    platform-level (super admins only)

**4.12.2 Audit Log Schema**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| CREATE TABLE audit_log (                                              |
|                                                                       |
| id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),                        |
|                                                                       |
| tenant_id UUID REFERENCES tenants(id), \-- NULL for platform-level    |
| events                                                                |
|                                                                       |
| scope VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL, \-- \'tenant\' \| \'platform\'            |
|                                                                       |
| actor_id UUID,                                                        |
|                                                                       |
| actor_email VARCHAR(255), \-- Denormalized --- user may be deleted    |
| later                                                                 |
|                                                                       |
| actor_role VARCHAR(50),                                               |
|                                                                       |
| actor_type VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL, \-- \'user\' \| \'system\' \|        |
| \'superadmin\' \| \'api\'                                             |
|                                                                       |
| actor_ip INET,                                                        |
|                                                                       |
| actor_user_agent TEXT,                                                |
|                                                                       |
| event_category VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,                                  |
|                                                                       |
| event_type VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,                                     |
|                                                                       |
| resource_type VARCHAR(50),                                            |
|                                                                       |
| resource_id UUID,                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| before_state JSONB,                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| after_state JSONB,                                                    |
|                                                                       |
| metadata JSONB,                                                       |
|                                                                       |
| entry_hash VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL, \-- SHA-256 of this entry\'s content |
|                                                                       |
| previous_hash VARCHAR(64), \-- Hash of previous entry in chain        |
|                                                                       |
| created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()                         |
|                                                                       |
| );                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.12.3 Event Taxonomy --- Six Categories**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Category**       **Key Events Captured**
  ------------------ -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1\. Authentication login_success, login_failed, logout, mfa_enabled/disabled, password_changed,
  & Access           account_locked, token_revoked, impersonation_started/ended

  2\. User &         user.created/deactivated/reactivated/role_changed/deleted,
  Permission         permission.override_set/removed
  Management         

  3\. Financial      invoice.created/submitted/approved/rejected/paid/voided,
  Events             change_order.issued/approved/rejected, budget.updated,
                     lien_waiver.issued/signed, contract.created/signed, payment.recorded

  4\. Project &      project.created/status_changed/deleted, task.status_changed,
  Operational Events inspection.submitted/failed, daily_report.submitted,
                     punch_list.item_created/resolved, schedule.milestone_changed,
                     rfi.created/responded, submittal.created/approved/rejected

  5\. Document &     document.uploaded/downloaded/deleted/scan_rejected/version_added
  File Events        

  6\. Cross-Tenant & connection.request_sent/accepted/declined/disconnected/permissions_changed,
  Platform Events    tenant.created/suspended/reactivated/cancelled/purged,
                     subscription.tier_changed, integration.connected/disconnected
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.12.4 Hash Chaining --- Tamper Evidence**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| function computeEntryHash(entry, previousHash) {                      |
|                                                                       |
| const content = JSON.stringify({                                      |
|                                                                       |
| tenant_id: entry.tenant_id, scope: entry.scope,                       |
|                                                                       |
| actor_id: entry.actor_id, actor_email: entry.actor_email,             |
|                                                                       |
| event_category: entry.event_category, event_type: entry.event_type,   |
|                                                                       |
| resource_type: entry.resource_type, resource_id: entry.resource_id,   |
|                                                                       |
| before_state: entry.before_state, after_state: entry.after_state,     |
|                                                                       |
| created_at: entry.created_at.toISOString(),                           |
|                                                                       |
| previous_hash: previousHash ?? \'GENESIS\',                           |
|                                                                       |
| });                                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| return crypto.createHash(\'sha256\').update(content).digest(\'hex\'); |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

A nightly background job verifies the hash chain. Any modification to a
past entry changes its hash, breaking the chain from that point forward
--- detectable immediately. Chain break triggers a critical security
alert.

**4.12.5 Retention Policy**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Scope**          **Retention**   **Rationale**
  ------------------ --------------- --------------------------------------
  Tenant audit log   7 years         Construction contract disputes and
                                     lien claims surface years after
                                     project completion

  Platform audit log 7 years         SOC 2 and internal security
                                     investigation requirements

  Authentication     7 years         Security investigation and compliance
  events                             

  Purged tenant data Audit log       actor_email denormalized --- legal
                     retained after  obligation survives data deletion
                     tenant purge    
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.13 Tenant Data Export**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Async ZIP archive. One CSV per domain plus all tenant files.
  Delivered via 7-day pre-signed URL. CCPA data portability compliant
  from v1.0 launch. --- T-35, T-36, T-37**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.13.1 Export Contents**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| export\_{tenant_id}\_{date}.zip                                       |
|                                                                       |
| ├── README.txt ← Field definitions, export date, platform version     |
|                                                                       |
| ├── data/                                                             |
|                                                                       |
| │ ├── projects.csv                                                    |
|                                                                       |
| │ ├── tasks.csv, users.csv, invoices.csv, change_orders.csv           |
|                                                                       |
| │ ├── contracts.csv, lien_waivers.csv, budget_lines.csv, payments.csv |
|                                                                       |
| │ ├── daily_reports.csv, inspections.csv, punch_list_items.csv        |
|                                                                       |
| │ ├── rfis.csv, submittals.csv, schedule_milestones.csv               |
|                                                                       |
| │ ├── vendors.csv, subcontractors.csv                                 |
|                                                                       |
| │ └── audit_log.csv ← Full 7-year audit history                       |
|                                                                       |
| └── files/                                                            |
|                                                                       |
| └── {project_id}/                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| ├── plans/                                                            |
|                                                                       |
| ├── photos/                                                           |
|                                                                       |
| └── documents/                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.13.2 Policies**

-   Maximum one active export job per tenant at a time

-   Download URL expires after 7 days --- tenant can request new export
    after expiry

-   Export files in storage deleted after 7 days via nightly cleanup job

-   Available during Active, Cancelled, and Grace Period states --- not
    after Purge

-   Tenant admin receives email with estimated completion time when job
    is enqueued

-   Tenant admin receives email with pre-signed download URL when export
    is ready

**4.14 Notification Infrastructure**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **APNs (iOS) + FCM (Android). Delivery fallback chain: in-app → push →
  email → SMS. Per-user preferences. Safety events cannot be disabled.
  --- T-38, T-39, T-40, T-41**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.14.1 Notification Channels**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Channel**    **Provider**          **Use Case**
  -------------- --------------------- ------------------------------------
  In-app         WebSocket             Real-time --- user is active in the
                 (Pusher/Ably)         app

  Push           APNs (iOS) + FCM      User is not active --- mobile
  notification   (Android)             background alert

  Email          SendGrid              Digest, important alerts, export
                                       delivery

  SMS            Twilio                Time-sensitive field alerts only ---
                                       user must opt in
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------

**4.14.2 Delivery Fallback Chain**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Is user currently active in app?                                      |
|                                                                       |
| ├── YES → Deliver via WebSocket (in-app) only                         |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| └── NO → Deliver push notification                                    |
|                                                                       |
| ├── Push delivered → Done                                             |
|                                                                       |
| └── Push fails / no device token                                      |
|                                                                       |
| └── Email fallback                                                    |
|                                                                       |
| └── SMS (high-priority events only)                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**4.14.3 Device Token Lifecycle**

-   Tokens upserted on every app launch --- handles token rotation
    automatically

-   APNs returns 410 Gone for expired tokens --- immediate deactivation

-   FCM returns UNREGISTERED for invalid tokens --- immediate
    deactivation

-   Platform never retries against a known-bad token

**4.14.4 Per-User Notification Preferences**

-   Per-channel opt-out: push_enabled, email_enabled, sms_enabled (SMS
    off by default --- user must opt in)

-   Per-category opt-out: task_updates, inspection_results,
    invoice_activity, change_orders, daily_reports, schedule_changes,
    document_uploads, rfis, payment_events

-   Safety events (notify_safety_events): cannot be disabled ---
    preference column exists but is ignored

-   Quiet hours: user-configurable local-time window where push and SMS
    are suppressed

**4.14.5 Notification Read/Unread State**

All notifications stored in notifications table. Unread count cached in
Redis per user for badge display. Unread count incremented on
notification creation, decremented on mark-read. All notifications
stored in user\'s preferred_language.

**5. Tenant Provisioning & Lifecycle**

**5.1 Real-Time Architecture & WebSocket Tenant Isolation**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **One private channel per tenant. Authorization endpoint validates JWT
  tenant_id against requested channel. Server fan-out for cross-tenant
  events. --- T-15, T-16, T-17**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**5.1.1 Channel Naming Convention**

  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Channel Type**   **Format**                   **Example**            **Who
                                                                         Subscribes**
  ------------------ ---------------------------- ---------------------- ---------------
  Tenant private     private-tenant-{tenant_id}   private-tenant-t_001   All
  channel                                                                authenticated
                                                                         users of that
                                                                         tenant

  Super admin        private-superadmin           private-superadmin     Super admin
  channel                                                                console only
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Channel names are never constructed from user-supplied input --- always
derived server-side from the validated JWT tenant_id claim. No public
channels exist on the platform.

**5.1.2 Channel Authorization Flow**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| // POST /v1/realtime/auth                                             |
|                                                                       |
| async function authorizeChannel(req, res) {                           |
|                                                                       |
| const { tenant_id, user_id } = req.jwt;                               |
|                                                                       |
| const { channel_name, socket_id } = req.body;                         |
|                                                                       |
| // Channel must match the requesting tenant --- no exceptions         |
|                                                                       |
| const expectedChannel = \`private-tenant-\${tenant_id}\`;             |
|                                                                       |
| if (channel_name !== expectedChannel) {                               |
|                                                                       |
| return res.status(403).json({ error: \'CHANNEL_FORBIDDEN\' });        |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| const authToken = pusher.authorizeChannel(socket_id, channel_name);   |
|                                                                       |
| return res.json(authToken);                                           |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**5.1.3 Standard Event Types**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Event**                     **Trigger**            **Channel**
  ----------------------------- ---------------------- -------------------------
  task.status_changed           Task updated           Tenant channel

  inspection.submitted          Inspection result      Tenant channel
                                submitted              

  daily_report.submitted        Daily report filed     Tenant channel

  invoice.status_changed        Invoice approved /     Tenant channel
                                rejected               

  change_order.issued           Change order created   Tenant channel

  notification.new              Any in-app             Tenant channel
                                notification           

  file.scan_complete            File scan result       Tenant channel
                                available              

  sync.conflict_detected        Offline sync conflict  Tenant channel

  connection.request_received   Cross-tenant           Tenant channel
                                connection invite      
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**5.1.4 Cross-Tenant Fan-Out Architecture**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Sub (t_002) completes task                                            |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| ▼                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| API writes to sub\'s DB tables (tenant_id = t_002)                    |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| ├──▶ Publish to private-tenant-t_002                                  |
|                                                                       |
| │ Full event payload                                                  |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| └──▶ shared_project_events record written                             |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| ▼                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| Fan-out service applies permission matrix                             |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| ▼                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| Publish to private-tenant-t_001 (GC)                                  |
|                                                                       |
| Scoped payload --- permitted fields only                              |
|                                                                       |
| (no internal cost data, no markup, no other jobs)                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

Both publishes happen in the same operation --- GC\'s dashboard updates
at the same moment as the sub\'s. The fan-out service applies the data
sharing permission matrix before constructing the GC payload.

**5.1.5 WebSocket Connection Limits**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Tier**        **Max Concurrent       **Behavior at Limit**
                  Connections**          
  --------------- ---------------------- ---------------------------------
  Starter         25                     New connections rejected ---
                                         client falls back to 30s polling

  Professional    100                    Same fallback

  Business        500                    Same fallback

  Enterprise      Unlimited              No limit enforced
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

**5.2 Self-Serve Tenant Provisioning Flow**

-   User visits signup page --- enters company name, email, password,
    trade type

-   Email verification sent --- user must verify before proceeding

-   Stripe customer created --- subscription initialized at selected
    tier

-   Tenant record created --- tenant_id (UUID) generated, slug created

-   Default data seeded: trade module, budget categories, quality
    checklists, document templates

-   Admin user record created and linked to tenant

-   Welcome email sent with onboarding wizard link

-   Tenant enters onboarding wizard --- company profile, first project,
    invite team, connect QuickBooks

Provisioning is fully automated. A new tenant goes from signup to first
active project in under 10 minutes.

**5.3 Tenant Lifecycle States**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **State**     **Description**          **Data Access**    **Billing**
  ------------- ------------------------ ------------------ --------------
  Trialing      14-day free trial ---    Full               No charge ---
                full Professional tier                      card required
                access                                      at signup

  Active        Paid subscription in     Full (within tier) Monthly or
                good standing                               annual via
                                                            Stripe

  Past Due      Payment failed --- grace Full --- grace     Retry logic
                period (7 days)          period             --- 3 attempts
                                                            over 7 days

  Suspended     Grace period expired --- Read-only --- no   Subscription
                payment unresolved       new data entry     paused

  Cancelled     Tenant cancelled         Read-only for 30   No further
                subscription             days               charges

  Purged        30 days                  None               None
                post-cancellation ---                       
                data deleted                                
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

**5.4 Data Retention & Deletion Policy**

-   On cancellation: tenant moves to read-only state for 30 days --- all
    data preserved

-   During 30-day grace period: tenant can reactivate and resume full
    access instantly

-   At day 30 post-cancellation: automated purge job deletes all tenant
    data from database and file storage

-   Purge is irreversible --- tenants warned via email at day 1, 7, 21,
    and 28

-   Tenant data export available at any time during active or
    cancelled/grace period states

-   Audit log entries are NEVER purged --- retained for 7 years even
    after tenant purge

**6. Cross-Tenant Collaboration Architecture**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **v1.1 Feature: Cross-tenant collaboration is NOT in v1.0. The database
  schema and API layer will be designed to accommodate it from day one,
  but the feature will not be activated until v1.1.**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**6.1 The Shared Project Layer Model**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| TENANT A (GC): ABC General Contractors \[tenant_id: t_001\]           |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| │ Project: Main Street Office Build \[project_id: p_100\]             |
|                                                                       |
| │ ├── Scope: Electrical (awarded to Smith Electric)                   |
|                                                                       |
| │ └── Scope: Plumbing (awarded to Martinez Plumbing)                  |
|                                                                       |
| │                                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| │ CONNECTION REQUEST ──────────────────────────────────┐              |
|                                                                       |
| │ │                                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| │ ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │               |
|                                                                       |
| │ │ SHARED PROJECT LAYER │ │                                          |
|                                                                       |
| │ │ \[shared_project_id: sp_200\] │ │                                 |
|                                                                       |
| │ │ Governed data bridge --- only permitted fields │ │                |
|                                                                       |
| │ └──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘ │               |
|                                                                       |
| │ │ │                                                                 |
|                                                                       |
| ▼ ▼ ▼                                                                 |
|                                                                       |
| GC Dashboard Shared View TENANT B (Sub): Smith Electrical             |
|                                                                       |
| (full project) (scoped) \[tenant_id: t_002\]                          |
|                                                                       |
| Own dashboard, own financials, own jobs                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**6.2 Cross-Tenant Connection Data Model**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| TABLE: tenant_connections                                             |
|                                                                       |
| id UUID PRIMARY KEY                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| initiating_tenant_id UUID FK -\> tenants(id) \-- GC tenant            |
|                                                                       |
| receiving_tenant_id UUID FK -\> tenants(id) \-- Sub tenant            |
|                                                                       |
| project_id UUID FK -\> projects(id) \-- The specific project          |
|                                                                       |
| scope_description TEXT                                                |
|                                                                       |
| contract_value DECIMAL(12,2)                                          |
|                                                                       |
| status VARCHAR(20) \-- pending \| active \| completed \| disconnected |
|                                                                       |
| initiated_at TIMESTAMPTZ                                              |
|                                                                       |
| accepted_at TIMESTAMPTZ                                               |
|                                                                       |
| permissions JSONB \-- Governs exactly what data crosses               |
|                                                                       |
| TABLE: shared_project_events                                          |
|                                                                       |
| id UUID PRIMARY KEY                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| connection_id UUID FK -\> tenant_connections(id)                      |
|                                                                       |
| event_type VARCHAR(50)                                                |
|                                                                       |
| source_tenant_id UUID                                                 |
|                                                                       |
| payload JSONB                                                         |
|                                                                       |
| created_at TIMESTAMPTZ                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**6.3 Data Sharing Permission Matrix**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Data Type**              **GC Sees** **Sub       **Shared (Both)**
                                         Sees**      
  -------------------------- ----------- ----------- ---------------------
  Sub\'s contract value with Yes         Yes         Yes --- this is the
  GC                                                 shared contract

  Sub\'s internal labor cost No          Yes         No --- private to Sub
  breakdown                                          

  Sub\'s markup / profit     No          Yes         No --- private to Sub
  margin                                             

  Sub\'s other active jobs / No          Yes         No --- private to Sub
  clients                                            

  Task completion status by  Yes         Yes         Yes --- core
  phase                                              collaboration data

  Inspection results and     Yes         Yes         Yes --- core
  photos                                             compliance data

  Daily field reports        Yes         Yes         Yes --- GC needs
  (sub\'s)                                           visibility

  Schedule for sub\'s scope  Yes         Yes         Yes --- shared
                                                     scheduling

  Change orders (sub\'s      Yes         Yes         Yes --- contract
  scope)                                             modification

  Sub\'s invoice to GC       Yes         Yes         Yes --- billing
                                                     workflow

  RFIs relevant to sub\'s    Yes         Yes         Yes --- design
  scope                                              clarifications

  GC\'s overall project      Yes         No          No --- private to GC
  budget                                             

  GC\'s other subcontractor  Yes         No          No --- private to GC
  costs                                              

  GC\'s client information   Yes         No          No --- private to GC
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

**6.4 Connection Workflow**

-   GC creates scope assignment on their project, selects a
    subcontractor

-   If sub\'s email domain matches an existing tenant, system flags
    potential platform connection

-   GC sends Connection Request --- sub receives email invite or in-app
    notification

-   Sub reviews proposed permissions and contract value, then accepts or
    declines

-   On acceptance: tenant_connection record created with status =
    \'active\'

-   Shared Project Layer instantiated --- sub\'s project dashboard shows
    this job

-   Both tenants see shared data in real time via server fan-out

-   At project closeout: either party can close connection --- shared
    data archived independently

**6.5 Non-Tenant Subcontractor Handling (Free Portal)**

If a sub is NOT a platform tenant, the GC can invite them to a free
limited portal. This sub gets a portal_user account. Portal users can:
view assigned scope and schedule, submit invoices, upload submittals,
respond to RFIs, submit daily field reports.

Portal users cannot create their own company environment, manage
independent projects, or access financial management tools. Their data
lives within the GC\'s tenant.

**6.6 Cross-Tenant Data Consistency**

-   Sub\'s action writes to their own tenant\'s tables normally
    (tenant_id = t_002)

-   A shared_project_events record is written simultaneously in the same
    transaction

-   The GC\'s dashboard reads from shared_project_events for the sub\'s
    scope --- never directly from sub\'s tables

-   Sub\'s data never lives in the GC\'s tenant tables --- no
    cross-tenant data ownership confusion

-   If the connection is closed, the GC retains the
    shared_project_events history --- the sub retains their own records

**6.7 shared_project_events Access Control**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **shared_project_events is explicitly exempt from standard tenant RLS.
  Access controlled at application layer via connection membership
  validation. --- T-44, T-45**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**6.7.1 Why Standard RLS Cannot Apply**

Rows are written by the sub\'s tenant context (tenant_id = t_002) but
must be readable by the GC\'s tenant context (tenant_id = t_001).
Standard policy WHERE tenant_id =
current_setting(\'app.current_tenant_id\') cannot satisfy both
requirements simultaneously.

**6.7.2 Resolution --- Exempt Table with Application-Layer Guard**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| \-- shared_project_events does NOT use standard tenant RLS            |
|                                                                       |
| ALTER TABLE shared_project_events DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;         |
|                                                                       |
| \-- Access controlled by dedicated roles                              |
|                                                                       |
| CREATE ROLE cross_tenant_reader;                                      |
|                                                                       |
| GRANT SELECT ON shared_project_events TO cross_tenant_reader;         |
|                                                                       |
| GRANT SELECT ON tenant_connections TO cross_tenant_reader;            |
|                                                                       |
| CREATE ROLE cross_tenant_writer;                                      |
|                                                                       |
| GRANT INSERT ON shared_project_events TO cross_tenant_writer;         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**6.7.3 Application-Layer Connection Validation**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| async function writeSharedEvent(connectionId, tenantId, eventType,    |
| payload) {                                                            |
|                                                                       |
| // Validate the writing tenant is a party to this connection          |
|                                                                       |
| const connection = await db.query(\`                                  |
|                                                                       |
| SELECT \* FROM tenant_connections                                     |
|                                                                       |
| WHERE id = \$1                                                        |
|                                                                       |
| AND (initiating_tenant_id = \$2 OR receiving_tenant_id = \$2)         |
|                                                                       |
| AND status = \'active\'                                               |
|                                                                       |
| \`, \[connectionId, tenantId\]);                                      |
|                                                                       |
| if (!connection) throw new                                            |
| AuthorizationError(\'UNAUTHORIZED_CONNECTION_WRITE\');                |
|                                                                       |
| await db.query(\`                                                     |
|                                                                       |
| INSERT INTO shared_project_events (connection_id, event_type,         |
| source_tenant_id, payload)                                            |
|                                                                       |
| VALUES (\$1, \$2, \$3, \$4)                                           |
|                                                                       |
| \`, \[connectionId, eventType, tenantId, payload\]);                  |
|                                                                       |
| }                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

All reads and writes to shared_project_events pass through connection
membership validation. Authorization failure throws immediately ---
never bypassed for performance. All cross-tenant access logged in audit
log.

**6.8 Portal User to Full Tenant Migration**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Portal user migration copies records to new tenant with new UUIDs.
  Soft-delete originals. Super admin approval required. --- T-46, T-47**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**6.8.1 The Data Ownership Problem**

Portal user data is created within the GC\'s tenant (tenant_id = t_001).
When the portal user subscribes and becomes a full tenant, they want
this history in their own environment. Re-stamping tenant_id on existing
rows is prohibited by RLS and would corrupt the GC\'s records.

**6.8.2 Migration Approach --- Copy, Don\'t Re-Stamp**

Portal data is copied to the new tenant with new UUIDs and the new
tenant_id. Original records in the GC tenant are soft-deleted (marked as
migrated --- not purged). Cross-references between copied records are
re-mapped to the new UUIDs. The entire migration runs in a single
database transaction with pre- and post-migration validation.

**6.8.3 Migratable Domains**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Domain**      **What Migrates**          **GC Record After Migration**
  --------------- -------------------------- -----------------------------
  daily_reports   All reports authored by    Soft-deleted, marked
                  portal user                migrated_to_tenant_id

  invoices        All invoices submitted by  Soft-deleted
                  portal user                

  file_uploads    All files uploaded by      Soft-deleted --- files copied
                  portal user                in storage

  inspections     Inspection results filed   Soft-deleted
                  by portal user             

  submittals      Submittals uploaded by     Soft-deleted
                  portal user                
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

Project records, schedule data, and contract records are NOT migrated
--- these belong to the GC\'s project environment. Migration requires
super admin approval and execution --- not self-serve. Full audit trail
logged as platform-scope events.

**7. Super Admin Layer**

The Super Admin console is a separate, secured application accessible
only to \[PLATFORM NAME\] platform operators. It sits above all tenant
environments and is accessed via a separate subdomain
(admin.platformname.com) with its own authentication system ---
completely separate from the tenant login flow.

**7.1 Super Admin Capabilities**

  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Capability**            **Description**
  ------------------------- ------------------------------------------------
  Tenant management         View all tenants, subscription status, user
                            counts, storage usage, creation date

  Tenant provisioning       Manually create or configure tenants for
                            enterprise/sales-assisted onboarding

  Tenant                    Suspend or reactivate tenants --- e.g. for
  suspension/reactivation   payment issues or policy violations

  Billing management        View Stripe subscription details, manually apply
                            credits, override billing

  Feature flag control      Enable or disable platform features globally or
                            per tenant

  Impersonation (read-only) View a tenant\'s environment as a read-only
                            observer for support --- cannot modify data

  Global template           Manage the global library of trade checklists,
  management                document templates, and workflows

  Usage analytics           Platform-wide: tenant count, active users, API
                            call volume, storage consumption, revenue
                            metrics

  Infrastructure health     Real-time status of database, API, storage,
                            integration services, and circuit breaker states

  Audit log (platform-wide) Cross-tenant audit log for security events and
                            support investigations

  Integration health        Real-time visibility into which integrations are
  dashboard                 degraded across the platform

  Failed webhook log        Inspectable and replayable webhook DLQ entries
                            with full raw payload

  Client version            Dashboard showing distribution of active mobile
  distribution              and web app versions

  Portal user migration     Approve and execute portal user to full tenant
                            data migrations

  Chain integrity status    Audit log hash chain verification status ---
                            nightly report
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------

**7.2 Super Admin Security Requirements**

-   Separate authentication system --- no shared session with tenant
    login

-   Hardware MFA required (FIDO2/WebAuthn) for all super admin accounts

-   IP allowlisting --- super admin access restricted to known IP ranges

-   All super admin actions logged with user, timestamp, and action
    detail

-   Impersonation sessions are time-limited (30 minutes max), read-only,
    and always logged

-   No super admin can access the super admin system from a tenant user
    account --- separate credentials required

**8. Security Architecture**

**8.1 Encryption**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Data State**     **Standard**        **Implementation**
  ------------------ ------------------- ----------------------------------------
  Data in transit    TLS 1.3             Enforced at API Gateway --- no HTTP
                                         allowed, HSTS headers set

  Data at rest       AES-256             Cloud provider managed encryption at
  (database)                             storage layer

  Data at rest (file AES-256             S3/Spaces server-side encryption on all
  storage)                               buckets

  Sensitive fields   AES-256             SSN, EIN, bank account data encrypted at
  (PII, financial)   application-layer   application layer with tenant-specific
                                         keys before DB write

  Backup data        AES-256             Automated backups inherit storage
                                         encryption --- backup access logged
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**8.2 Authentication Security**

-   Passwords: bcrypt with cost factor 12 minimum --- never stored in
    plain text

-   Account lockout: 5 failed login attempts triggers 15-minute lockout
    with email alert

-   MFA: TOTP authenticator app --- optional per user, enforceable by
    tenant admin

-   Session management: JWT with short expiry + refresh token rotation

-   Token revocation: real-time via Redis jti blacklist

**8.3 API Security**

-   All API endpoints require authentication --- no unauthenticated
    endpoints except login and signup

-   Role-based access control enforced at the service layer --- not just
    the route layer

-   Input validation: all API inputs validated and sanitized ---
    parameterized queries only

-   CORS: strict origin allowlisting --- no wildcard CORS

-   Rate limiting: per-tenant limits enforced at API Gateway

-   SQL injection: impossible by design --- ORM-based queries with
    parameterized inputs only

-   File upload: triple validation (extension + magic bytes +
    Content-Type) before storage write

-   File download: pre-signed URLs only --- 15-minute expiry, never
    direct storage path exposure

**8.4 Compliance Roadmap**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Standard**    **Target         **Priority**
                  Timeline**       
  --------------- ---------------- ---------------------------------------
  SOC 2 Type I    12 months        High --- required for Enterprise sales.
                  post-launch      Audit log (Sec 4.12) begins collecting
                                   evidence at v1.0 launch.

  SOC 2 Type II   18--24 months    High --- required for large GC and
                  post-launch      enterprise customers

  GDPR readiness  Before any EU    Medium --- not required for US/Canada
                  market entry     v1.0 launch

  CCPA compliance v1.0 launch      Required --- California customers from
                                   day one. Data export (Sec 4.13)
                                   satisfies portability requirement.

  PCI DSS         v1.0 launch      Stripe handles card data --- platform
  (payments)                       never touches raw card numbers; Stripe
                                   is PCI DSS Level 1
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

**8.5 Security Testing**

-   Automated security scanning in CI/CD pipeline --- run on every pull
    request

-   Dependency vulnerability scanning --- npm audit, Snyk, or Dependabot

-   Static application security testing (SAST) --- detect common
    vulnerabilities in code

-   Tenant isolation penetration test --- before beta launch

-   Full penetration test --- before v1.0 public launch

-   Quarterly penetration tests post-launch

-   PgBouncer tenant context isolation test --- against staging config
    before any production deployment (see Sec 3.7.3)

**9. Infrastructure & Deployment**

**9.1 Staged Infrastructure Plan**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **The platform launches on DigitalOcean. AWS migration triggered at
  300+ tenants or first enterprise customer requiring SOC 2. Migration
  requires 1--2 sprints --- no architectural rework. --- T-24**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**9.1.1 Stage 1 --- Pre-Revenue / Design Partners (0--50 Tenants)**

Provider: DigitalOcean \| Target monthly cost: \~\$200--350

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Component**      **DigitalOcean Service** **Spec**
  ------------------ ------------------------ ---------------------------
  API servers        App Platform             2 containers, 1vCPU/1GB
                     (containers)             each

  Database           Managed PostgreSQL       db-s-2vcpu-4gb, daily
                                              backups, 1 standby node

  Cache              Managed Redis            db-s-1vcpu-1gb

  File storage       Spaces (S3-compatible)   Per-tenant prefix ---
                                              identical path structure to
                                              S3

  CDN                Spaces CDN               Static assets and plan file
                                              delivery

  Background workers App Platform workers     Same container, worker
                                              role. pg-boss for job
                                              queue.

  Email              SendGrid free tier       Up to 100 emails/day

  Real-time          Pusher Sandbox           Free up to 200 connections

  File scanning      Cloudmersive Virus Scan  Free tier --- 800
                     API                      scans/month

  Monitoring         DigitalOcean built-in +  Basic metrics + error
                     Sentry free              tracking
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**9.1.2 Stage 2 --- Early Revenue (50--300 Tenants)**

Provider: DigitalOcean (scaled) \| Target monthly cost: \~\$500--700

-   Scale to 4--6 API containers, larger instances

-   Upgrade database to db-s-4vcpu-8gb, add 1 read replica

-   Migrate background jobs to dedicated worker fleet

-   Pusher Growth plan (\~\$100/month), SendGrid Essentials
    (\~\$25/month)

-   Add Datadog --- 3 hosts (\~\$75/month)

**9.1.3 Stage 3 --- Growth (300--500 Tenants) --- AWS Migration**

Provider: Amazon Web Services \| Target monthly cost: \~\$1,000--1,200

Migration triggered when any condition is met: 300+ active paying
tenants, enterprise customer requires SOC 2 Type I, DigitalOcean standby
failover insufficient for customer SLA commitments, or Cloudmersive
pricing unfavorable vs GuardDuty.

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Component**      **DigitalOcean → AWS**         **Code Change
                                                    Required?**
  ------------------ ------------------------------ ---------------------
  PostgreSQL         Managed PostgreSQL → RDS       None --- same
                     PostgreSQL Multi-AZ            Postgres, same RLS

  Redis              Managed Redis → ElastiCache    None --- same Redis
                                                    API

  File storage       Spaces → S3                    None --- Spaces is
                                                    S3-compatible. Swap
                                                    endpoint env var.

  CDN                Spaces CDN → CloudFront        Minor --- update
                                                    asset URL config

  Containers         App Platform → ECS Fargate     None --- same Docker
                                                    containers

  Background jobs    pg-boss → SQS + Lambda         Low --- job envelope
                                                    structure unchanged,
                                                    queue client swaps

  File scanning      Cloudmersive → GuardDuty       Low --- swap scanning
                                                    provider in upload
                                                    handler

  Monitoring         Sentry + DO → Datadog +        None --- add
                     CloudWatch                     CloudWatch alongside

  Connection pooling Built-in → PgBouncer on ECS    Low --- add PgBouncer
                                                    container, update DB
                                                    connection string
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**9.1.4 Stage 4 --- Scale (500--2,500 Tenants)**

Provider: AWS (scaled) \| Target monthly cost: \~\$2,400

Standard AWS scaling playbook --- additional read replicas, larger RDS
instance, expanded ECS cluster. No architectural changes required until
2,500+ tenants, at which point table partitioning by tenant_id is
evaluated for the largest tables.

**9.1.5 Infrastructure Decisions That Are Stage-Invariant**

These work identically on DigitalOcean and AWS regardless of stage:

-   PostgreSQL RLS with SET LOCAL app.current_tenant_id

-   UUID primary keys

-   Per-tenant storage prefix isolation --- path structure identical

-   JWT structure and token lifecycle

-   withTenantContext() wrapper pattern

-   Exponential backoff retry strategy

-   Circuit breaker pattern (Redis-backed)

**9.2 Core AWS Infrastructure Components (Stage 3+)**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Component**         **AWS Service**       **Purpose**
  --------------------- --------------------- ----------------------------
  Application servers   ECS (Fargate) or EC2  Stateless API containers ---
                        Auto Scaling          horizontally scalable

  Database              RDS PostgreSQL        Primary database with
                        (Multi-AZ)            automatic failover standby

  Read replicas         RDS Read Replicas     1 read replica at launch ---
                                              scaled up as reporting load
                                              grows

  Caching               ElastiCache (Redis)   Session tokens, rate
                                              limiting, tenant config,
                                              dashboard caches

  File storage          S3                    All tenant documents, plans,
                                              photos --- per-tenant prefix
                                              isolation

  CDN                   CloudFront            Global delivery of static
                                              assets, plan files, and
                                              images

  Background jobs       SQS + Lambda or ECS   Async tasks: QuickBooks
                        tasks                 sync, email delivery, report
                                              generation

  File scanning         GuardDuty Malware     Automated S3 object scanning
                        Protection            --- triggers on PutObject to
                                              quarantine prefix

  Email delivery        SendGrid (via API)    Transactional email ---
                                              maintained for
                                              deliverability and analytics

  SMS                   Twilio                Crew and client SMS
                                              notifications

  Push notifications    APNs + FCM            iOS and Android push
                                              delivery

  Load balancer         Application Load      HTTPS termination, health
                        Balancer (ALB)        checks, request distribution

  DNS                   Route 53              Domain management, failover
                                              routing

  Secrets management    AWS Secrets Manager   API keys, database
                                              credentials, integration
                                              tokens --- never hardcoded

  Monitoring            CloudWatch + Datadog  Infrastructure metrics,
                                              application performance,
                                              error tracking, alerting

  Logging               CloudWatch Logs +     Centralized application and
                        OpenSearch            audit logging with search
                                              capability
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------

**9.3 Availability & Disaster Recovery**

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Scenario**       **Strategy**                   **RTO**     **RPO**
  ------------------ ------------------------------ ----------- -------------
  Single AZ failure  Multi-AZ RDS automatic         \< 2        0 ---
                     failover, ALB routes around    minutes     synchronous
                     unhealthy instances                        standby

  Database           Point-in-time recovery from    \< 1 hour   5 minutes
  corruption         automated backups (retained 30             
                     days)                                      

  Region-wide outage Manual failover to backup      \< 4 hours  15 minutes
                     region (warm standby) --- S3               
                     cross-region replication                   

  Accidental data    30-day backup retention ---    \< 2 hours  5 minutes
  deletion           restore to point before                    
                     deletion                                   
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

**9.4 CI/CD Pipeline**

-   All code changes require pull request review --- no direct pushes to
    main

-   Automated test suite runs on every PR: unit tests, integration
    tests, tenant isolation tests

-   Security scanning on every PR --- SAST, dependency vulnerability
    check

-   PgBouncer tenant context isolation test runs against staging before
    any production deployment

-   Staging environment mirrors production --- every release deployed to
    staging first

-   Database migrations run automatically via migration tool (Flyway or
    Liquibase) --- versioned, reversible

-   Blue/green or rolling deployments for zero-downtime releases

-   Feature flags control new feature rollout --- deploy code before
    enabling for tenants

