                     Elasticsearch,       launch --- sufficient Lead
                     Typesense            for v1.0. Typesense   
                                          if needed at scale.   

  Background jobs    pg-boss, BullMQ, Que pg-boss ---           Engineering
  (Stage 1--2)       (Ruby)               PostgreSQL-backed, no Lead
                                          additional            
                                          infrastructure, clean 
                                          migration to SQS at   
                                          Stage 3               
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Critical Note on Connection Pooling + RLS: PgBouncer must be
  configured in transaction mode (not session mode) when using PostgreSQL
  RLS with SET LOCAL for tenant context. In session mode, connections are
  reused across requests and tenant context bleeds between sessions.
  Transaction mode resets SET LOCAL on each transaction --- ensuring
  isolation. Validate this configuration before any data is written to
  production. (See Section 3.7)**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**12. Internationalization Architecture**

i18n is architected as a first-class concern across all layers. The goal
is that adding a new language in v1.1 or v2.0 requires translation files
only --- no code changes, no schema migrations, no frontend component
updates.

**12.1 Frontend i18n Stack (Web + Mobile)**

  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Component**      **Technology**                **Configuration**
  ------------------ ----------------------------- -------------------------
  i18n library       react-i18next (web + React    Same library, same API,
                     Native)                       same translation key
                                                   namespace on both
                                                   platforms

  Translation file   JSON --- one file per         Namespace structure:
  format             language per namespace        common.json,
                                                   schedule.json,
                                                   financials.json,
                                                   field.json, portal.json,
                                                   notifications.json,
                                                   safety.json

  Locale detection   navigator.language →          User preference always
  --- web            user.preferred_language →     wins over browser default
                     tenant.default_language →     
                     \'en\'                        

  Locale detection   expo-localization.locale →    Device locale detected on
  --- mobile         user.preferred_language →     first launch. User can
                     \'en\'                        override in Profile \>
                                                   Language.

  Lazy loading       Translations loaded by        Field screens load
                     namespace on demand           field.json; financial
                                                   screens load
                                                   financials.json. Reduces
                                                   bundle size.

  Date formatting    Intl.DateTimeFormat(locale,   en-US: March 13, 2026 \|
                     options)                      es: 13 de marzo de 2026

  Number formatting  Intl.NumberFormat(locale,     Decimal separator: period
                     {style: \'decimal\'})         (en-US) vs comma (es,
                                                   pt-BR). Handled
                                                   automatically.

  Currency           Intl.NumberFormat(locale,     All monetary amounts
  formatting         {style: \'currency\',         display in user\'s locale
                     currency: \'USD\'})           format. Wire format
                                                   always in cents.

  RTL support        CSS logical properties        Arabic (v2.0+) RTL layout
                     throughout                    enabled by adding
                                                   dir=\'rtl\' to root ---
                                                   no component rewrites
                                                   needed
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------

**12.2 Translation File Structure**

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| /locales                                                              |
|                                                                       |
| /en                                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| common.json ← buttons, labels, status values, navigation              |
|                                                                       |
| field.json ← daily reports, inspections, punch list, clock-in         |
|                                                                       |
| schedule.json ← Gantt, tasks, milestones, delays                      |
|                                                                       |
| financials.json ← invoices, change orders, lien waivers, budget       |
|                                                                       |
| notifications.json ← all push, email, SMS message templates           |
|                                                                       |
| safety.json ← safety warnings, incident reports, hazard labels        |
|                                                                       |
| portal.json ← client portal + sub portal                              |
|                                                                       |
| /es ← mirrors /en structure --- same keys, Spanish values             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

**12.3 Backend Locale Handling**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Layer**          **Implementation**
  ------------------ ----------------------------------------------------
  Accept-Language    All API requests include Accept-Language header.
  header             Backend uses this for server-rendered content,
                     notification templates, and error message locale.

  User locale        preferred_language VARCHAR(10) stored on users
  preference         table. Set at signup or in Profile settings. Takes
                     precedence over Accept-Language header.

  Notification       When queuing a notification, the service reads
  delivery           recipient.preferred_language and selects the correct
                     template from the notifications.json namespace.

  Error messages     API error responses include a localized message
                     field in the user\'s language alongside the
                     machine-readable error.code.

  Audit log          Audit log entries always stored in English
                     regardless of user locale --- never translate stored
                     audit data.
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**12.4 Translation Management Pipeline**

-   Phrase (or Lokalise) integrated with GitHub CI --- new i18n keys in
    a PR auto-create translation tasks

-   English source file is the single source of truth --- all other
    languages are derived

-   Professional human translators for: safety content, legal
    terminology, field-worker UI, notification templates

-   DeepL machine translation acceptable for: internal admin text,
    low-stakes labels --- human review before merge

-   Native speaker QA required for each new language before GA ---
    construction-domain knowledge required

-   Spanish string freeze 30 days before v1.0 launch --- translation and
    QA complete before code freeze

